+# Ralue application integration contract
+
+The application remains a WOPI host. Ralue Editor is a stateless document
+engine and must not become the source of truth for files, versions, users, or
+permissions.
+
+## Preferred environment variables
+
+```text
+NEXT_PUBLIC_RALUE_EDITOR_ORIGIN=https://editor.example.com
+RALUE_EDITOR_INTERNAL_ORIGIN=http://ralue-editor:9980
+NEXT_PUBLIC_WOPI_PUBLIC_BASE=https://app.example.com
+```
+
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_COLLABORA_ORIGIN`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_COLLABORA_BASE`, and
+`COLLABORA_INTERNAL_ORIGIN` are migration fallbacks only. New deployments use
+the Ralue names.
+
+## Application routes
+
+- `/ralue-editor/*` is the branded proxy route.
+- `/collabora/*` remains as a temporary backward-compatible alias.
+- `/browser/*`, `/cool/*`, `/lool/*`, and `/hosting/*` preserve the engine and
+  WebSocket contracts expected by existing WOPI sessions.
+
+## Parent application touch points
+
+The Career Hub application integration is intentionally small:
+
+- `next.config.js`: prefer Ralue origins and expose the branded proxy alias;
+- `docker-compose.yml`: run `ralue/editor:mvp-26.04.2.4` as `ralue-editor`;
+- `app/pdf-editor/[key]/page.tsx` and `app/cover-letter/[key]/page.tsx`: prefer
+  the Ralue public origin and use the Ralue purple CSS variable;
+- `app/api/preview/pdf/route.ts`: use the server-side Ralue origin for PDF
+  conversion;
+- `.env.example`: document new variables while retaining migration fallbacks.
+
+Do not rename WOPI message IDs or `/cool` protocol routes. Internal legacy
+identifiers can be migrated separately after all existing sessions and tests
+have moved to the branded contract.
+
+## Verification order
+
+1. Check `/hosting/discovery` and `/hosting/capabilities`.
+2. Open an authenticated DOCX through the application.
+3. Edit, save, close, and reopen it; verify the immutable WOPI version changed.
+4. Open a second session and verify both users appear.
+5. Restart the editor container and verify the saved version reopens.
+6. Convert the active DOCX to PDF and inspect the rendered page.
+
+The parent application can have unrelated TypeScript failures. A failure in an
+unrelated route must not invalidate the editor image if the integration checks
+above pass; record both results separately.
